{
    "background_story": "Kolton was a talented painter, but his artistic genius was often overshadowed by his glum demeanor. He had a habit of getting lost in his own thoughts, and his introspective nature made him come across as aloof to those who didn't know him. Kolton's art studio was a reflection of his mood - dimly lit, with canvases that seemed to absorb the little light that filtered in. Despite his gloomy exterior, Kolton's paintings were vibrant and expressive, a testament to the turmoil that brewed beneath his reserved surface. His glumness was a shield, a way to protect himself from the world's expectations and criticisms. Few people got to see the dry wit and sharp humor that lay hidden beneath, but those who did were rewarded with a loyal and thoughtful friend.",
